ich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P(P(∅))={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P(P({∅}))={∅,{∅}}$\n- **III.** $P(P({0}))={∅,{∅},{{0}},{∅,{0}}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the power set of the set $∅$ is ${∅}.$ Therefore, $P(P(∅))={∅,{∅}}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{∅}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({∅}))={∅,{∅},{{∅}},{∅,{∅}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that we are given the set ${0}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{0}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({0}))={∅,{∅},{{0}},{∅,{0}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a45469e-136a-5e5b-b99c-d0986cc05aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471209} {:answer/id #uuid "34298241-b946-5a36-9d6f-cdccc915da9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a45469e-136a-5e5b-b99c-d0986cc05aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471209} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5ec5c4-62cb-56d9-bab7-8189327c57a5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bc87f60-846a-5297-91f2-4b0d573ccaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471211} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c37cf-9e89-5f2f-836e-fe89e922b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c37cf-9e89-5f2f-836e-fe89e922b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471212} :answer-field/id #uuid "7348f3ad-5c47-51b6-adc0-96ac7ad27556" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e69bd74-d6db-5f41-aaba-1646f9178cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471213} {:answer/id #uuid "c008f84e-6f4f-5a9b-bf98-a8afad9a4478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e69bd74-d6db-5f41-aaba-1646f9178cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471213} :answer-field/id #uuid "68fd73fa-c23e-5720-9d17-1ef1a6a7e99e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afe01a46-709c-5c6f-b721-547dd77ac300" :question/math-academy-id "q-182244" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P(P(2))={∅,{2}}$\n- **II.** $P(P({2}))={∅,{∅},{{2}},{∅,{2}}}$\n- **III.** $P(P({{2}}))={∅,{{2}}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that $2$ is not a set. So, the notation $P(P(2))$ does not make sense.\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that we are given the set ${2}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{2}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({2}))={∅,{∅},{{2}},{∅,{2}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that we are given the set ${{2}}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{{2}}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({{2}}))={∅,{∅},{{{2}}},{∅,{{2}}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4823cf5-2656-5616-b4af-193f70c3f2bc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Euler's Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f66501b7-d67d-50cf-a4c7-0e7ded793fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471395} {:answer/id #uuid "6965fa1e-0340-523a-974b-940af0fc110a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6965fa1e-0340-523a-974b-940af0fc110a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471396} :answer-field/id #uuid "261d3c79-9b7c-5247-a9e0-edbf257b665c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87945c09-3271-5a68-a1bf-3fcb83af70d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471397} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbd88b6-df12-5510-a648-3f66f69dc86e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87945c09-3271-5a68-a1bf-3fcb83af70d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471397} :answer-field/id #uuid "af459ec0-4cc0-52d7-9eb0-3dde1622afa9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3779885c-b90e-52f5-a5f2-b3c21d40229b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471399} {:answer/id #uuid "57ab8460-a824-5d98-aebd-b0482caac27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57ab8460-a824-5d98-aebd-b0482caac27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471400} :answer-field/id #uuid "faf4f041-9d66-5c32-91ff-4106fe85d773" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1f2baf0-4b87-5c2b-9ea5-eeef4731f725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471401} {:answer/id #uuid "09474881-68d0-5b18-95f0-b3882e547c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f2baf0-4b87-5c2b-9ea5-eeef4731f725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471401} :answer-field/id #uuid "06f4b1d1-82b6-5b27-958b-7d47672530ae" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7357f0db-ce2b-5133-a2b6-cf34bdf9d888" :question/math-academy-id "q-334012" :question/problem "For which of the following step sizes is Euler's Method **unstable**, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda >0,$ and step size $Δx?$\n- **I.** $Δx=\\frac{2.5}{\\lambda }$\n- **II.** $Δx=\\frac{0.6}{\\lambda }$\n- **III.** $Δx=\\frac{3}{\\lambda }$\n- **IV.** $Δx=\\frac{1.9}{\\lambda }$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function for Euler's method is given by $R(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nFor stability, we require that the following condition holds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(\\lambda Δx)| & <1 \\\\ |1-\\lambda Δx| & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this gives\n\n$$\n0<\\lambda Δx<2.\n$$\n\nThis means that Euler's method is stable when applied to the test equation for values in the region $0<\\lambda Δx<2.$\n\nNow, we consider each step size in turn.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{2.5}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=2.5\\ge 2.$ Since this value falls outside the given region, Euler's method is not stable (or unstable) for this step size.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{0.6}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=0.6.$ Since this value falls within the given region,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & <\\lambda Δx<2 \\\\ 0 & <0.6<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEuler's method must be stable for this step size.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{3}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=3\\ge 2.$ Since this value falls outside the given region, Euler's method is not stable (or unstable) for this step size.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{1.9}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=1.9.$ Since this value falls within the given region,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & <\\lambda Δx<2 \\\\ 0 & <1.9<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEuler's method must be stable for this step size.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372670 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4823cf5-2656-5616-b4af-193f70c3f2bc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Euler's Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "366d8acf-79b7-5e71-9b0d-049e02cb0fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471403} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce1e8fa-d6aa-5d53-8c65-6c893ade9430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "366d8acf-79b7-5e71-9b0d-049e02cb0fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471403} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3e43d5-60c1-55d5-a665-f4184d96dd42" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55e12b5c-4eaa-50c7-8d9e-a394ac5ce0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471405} {:answer/id #uuid "adeaf175-81b3-562a-88d9-68b0a9c47518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55e12b5c-4eaa-50c7-8d9e-a394ac5ce0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471405} :answe