4178" :question/problem "For which of the following values is Euler's method **unstable**, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda >0,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\nI. $\\lambda Δx=0.5$\n\nII. $\\lambda Δx=1.8$\n\nIII. $\\lambda Δx=2.1$\n\nIV. $\\lambda Δx=3$\n\n*Hint: The stability function for Euler's method is given by* $R(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nFor stability, we require that the following condition holds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(\\lambda Δx)| & <1 \\\\ |1-\\lambda Δx| & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this gives\n\n$$\n0<\\lambda Δx<2.\n$$\n\nThis means that Euler's method is stable when applied to the test equation for values in the region $0<\\lambda Δx<2.$ Of the given values:\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.5,$ falls *within* the given region,\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.8,$ falls *within* the given region,\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.1,$ falls *outside* the given region.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3,$ falls *outside* the given region.\n\nHence, Euler's method is **unstable** for the values $\\lambda Δx=2.1,$ and $\\lambda Δx=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III and IV only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a236ee0f-4a3d-55a5-9a29-b092842930da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471419} {:answer/id #uuid "4450a753-5992-5151-b771-796d2894c70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4450a753-5992-5151-b771-796d2894c70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471420} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7700a96-7ad6-5083-ad7c-8e281c670000" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472215} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9763120-6606-599b-934b-95db763e1233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471421} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4cc027-2dc9-5355-9d88-5ae327c54cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b4cc027-2dc9-5355-9d88-5ae327c54cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471422} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e42b658-9bec-5e39-bc22-0ea6b0feedc4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f648fda4-e87f-566a-a566-4e09bc924214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471423} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea37cf6-6012-5d5e-84a5-417006c11a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f648fda4-e87f-566a-a566-4e09bc924214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471423} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8e99c3d-6364-5eaf-82d2-dbbe369ebad8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472217} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a41646e7-d2e0-53ec-8d1a-a1a417903331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471425} {:answer/id #uuid "01fd0090-091c-5732-9466-b423e9e87912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a41646e7-d2e0-53ec-8d1a-a1a417903331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471425} :answer-field/id #uuid "1852daa2-566c-5147-b4a4-9116977c2ae4" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd6bd92c-8765-5d3c-9d52-912010fd3181" :question/math-academy-id "q-334425" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the Runge-Kutta Method (RK4) stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n- **I.** $\\lambda Δx=0.3$\n- **II.** $\\lambda Δx=2.4$\n- **III.** $\\lambda Δx=2.8$\n- **IV.** $\\lambda Δx=3$\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the RK4 method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{4}}{24}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method  ${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$ is stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the RK4 Method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{4}}{24}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the RK4 Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.3)| & =|1-0.3+\\frac{(0.3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(0.3)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(0.3)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{59\\,267}{80\\,000}| \\\\  & =0.740…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(2.4)| & =|1-2.4+\\frac{(2.4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(2.4)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(2.4)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{349}{625}| \\\\  & =0.558…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(2.8)| & =|1-2.8+\\frac{(2.8)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(2.8)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(2.8)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{639}{625}| \\\\  & =1.0224>1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *outside* the stability region, the RK4 Method is unstable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(3)| & =|1-3+\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(3)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(3)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{11}{8}| \\\\  & =1.375<1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *outside* the stability region, the RK4 Method is unstable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".\n\nNote that the stability region of the RK4 Method is $0<\\lambda Δx<2.785…,$ so it is not absolutely stable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcfddc24-c58f-5c4f-84e9-ef551982185b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471427} {:answer/id #uuid "9769274f-fb36-5fbc-8541-fc90883166a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9769274f-fb36-5fbc-8541-fc90883166a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471428} :answer-field/id #uuid "41a7fbf7-0d41-5041-aae1-a39e147b182f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f185f3b-0a68-5abd-a8c2-38bf014f58b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471429} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8a98cb-e1a9-56a3-92c7-055782d9153d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa8a98cb-e1a9-56a3-92c7-055782d9153d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471430} :answer-field/id #uuid "74f644d8-2edd-5b0b-937d-f2bfddc4567b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088c5cde-2edc-582f-8a1e-928e3b8226d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471431} {:answer/id #uuid "dfda1d96-e20f-55b1-8aa9-981ec2a0f203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "088c5cde-2edc-582f-8a1e-928e3b8226d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471431} :answer-field/id #uuid "79254c88-eae6-5edf-bb54-1cc11619fc3f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753fff6f-e13f-5c5d-ae71-087ae88e049e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471433} {:answer/id #uuid "e59e1c38-8632-55cd-89ae-49999007c409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e59e1c38-8632-55cd-89ae-49999007c409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471434} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b3380c0-50d4-5961-9f40-7aaca9597d4f" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ea2a49c-9462-54d3-b8e9-50d1002b7880" :question/math-academy-id "q-334775" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the modified Euler method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n- **I.** $\\lambda Δx=0.65$\n- **II.** $\\lambda Δx=1.35$\n- **III.** $\\lambda Δx=3.6$\n- **IV.** $\\lambda Δx=1.25$\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the modified Euler method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the modified Euler method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the modified Euler method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.65,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.65)| & =|1-0.65+\\frac{(0.65)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{449}{800}| \\\\  & =0.561\\,25<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the modified Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.35,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.35)| & =|1-1.35+\\frac{(1.35)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{449}{800}| \\\\  & =0.561\\,25<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the modified Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3.6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(3.6)| & =|1-3.6+\\frac{(3.6)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{97}{25}| \\\\  & =3.88>1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *outside* the stability region, the modified Euler method is unstable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.25)| & =|1-1.25+\\frac{(1.25)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{17}{32}| \\\\  & =0.531\\,25<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Since this value falls *within* the stability region, the modified Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only\".\n\nNote that the stability region of the modified Euler method is $0<\\lambda Δx<2,$ so it is not absolutely stable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de1b2908-d140-5d0a-8262-c958d76bfa4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471471} {:answer/id #uuid "f456143a-b430-5e18-95eb-88219103f545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de1b2908-d140-5d0a-8262-c958d76bfa4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471471} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e697f7-446e-5fcc-ae8a-db378503de70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55e41eb5-2115-5b1f-9bbb-e67f510d8e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471473} {:answer/id #uuid "bf770033-4a57-5465-a9ee-d6d68d54b733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf770033-4a57-5465-a9ee-d6d68d54b733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471474} :answer-field/id #uuid "83576e31-5a8a-5315-8054-127553d4c6a1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad5d90de-a61d-5e9f-a889-d499427c60be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471475} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5c3a1e-f107-5159-ae8f-6ce7a0d2da41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5d90de-a61d-5e9f-a889-d499427c60be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471475} :answer-field/id #uuid "5771a531-83c1-5b90-a459-0ec86b28bfd9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c853fbcf-5be0-5101-8f2a-558cbd4a782f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71402" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=9x+3y-4$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n- **II.** $c=-4$ gives a line\n- **III.** $c=5$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-4 & =c \\\\ 3y & =-9x+c+4 \\\\ y & =-3x+\\frac{c+4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+\\frac{4}{3},$ which is not an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=-4$ then the level curve is $y=-3x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=5$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+3,$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f674a4-7e0c-5322-95cd-c4b2362d53fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471161} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b723fe-a92e-5063-ace2-988c2fd6cc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4b723fe-a92e-5063-ace2-988c2fd6cc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471162} :answer-field/id #uuid "c71d614e-a737-553d-92b0-175cd68d4748" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472086} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b7f155-a99f-568b-9e4b-ea4955b52401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471163} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab61b8f-e7be-5407-806d-bbf75d626cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab61b8f-e7be-5407-806d-bbf75d626cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471164} :answer-field/id #uuid "227aaddd-09ce-5b40-8940-c72187069106" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "984d326c-9652-5ab5-978b-97b03286f0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471165} {:answer/id #uuid "332a5d32-f669-5ca5-9583-2148425f8f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "984d326c-9652-5ab5-978b-97b03286f0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471165} :answer-field/id #uuid "498b9449-b183-59dc-8461-4984778c1d56" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0311da7-2e05-528f-8234-394bbb366e6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-174352" :question/problem "Which of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?\n\nI. $\\{3,4,5\\}$ and $\\{6,7,8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{-4,-3,-2\\}$ and $\\{2,3,4\\}$\n\nIII. $[-3,0]$ and $[0,3]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Pair I is disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n\\{3,4,5\\}\\cap \\{6,7,8\\}=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Pair II is also disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n\\{-4,-3,-2\\}\\cap \\{2,3,4\\}=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Pair III is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n[-3,0]\\cap [0,3]=\\{0\\}\\ne ∅\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fe7defe-a71a-57a7-8f21-270ae5e67822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471167} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb77cda-2863-59bc-a98b-6353a74f96f6" :answer/type {:db/id 