x} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17f91135-f9d8-56cf-88b5-eaf7c61a4e5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86690" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n- **I.** $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$\n- **II.** $¬X∨(X∧¬Y)$\n- **III.** $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬X∧(X∨¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨(X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$ and $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e517c4-23a1-5dc9-9873-db08b9aeb3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470649} {:answer/id #uuid "9ade5b3f-5cb6-518d-a651-81454cda6151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e517c4-23a1-5dc9-9873-db08b9aeb3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 