ulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3546d6ca-c236-59ab-90e2-5cf833951b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103060" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $E?$\n- **I.** $F∧(F∨E)$\n- **II.** $E∧(F∨E)$\n- **III.** $E∨(F∨E)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nE∧(E∨F)≡E.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $E.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F∧(F∨E) & ≡F≢E.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $E.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E∧(F∨E) & ≡E∧(E∨F) \\\\  & ≡E.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $E.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a897efcf-c493-5598-9acc-bff660f4510e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470655} {:answer/id #uuid "0355f714-2a1a-5862-bd5e-c5aa32745c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0355f714-2a1a-5862-bd5e-c5aa32745c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470656} :answer-field/id #uuid "73d99ea3-1208-5bf6-b85d-273ae3953352" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471833} {:answer-field/choices [{