bs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nG∧(G∨H)≡G.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $G.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(H∨G)∧G & ≡G∧(H∨G) \\\\  & ≡G∧(G∨H) \\\\  & ≡G.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $G.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H∧(H∨G) & ≡H≢G.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $G.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb6e0931-7b46-55a9-aedc-7e3c239f2548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470661} {:answer/id #uuid "93e7930e-b8e0-5b4e-9f37-e812ddbbf78e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb6e0931-7b46-55a9-aedc-7e3c239f2548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470661} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac6cee7-69ab-56c7-aabd-58768c438222" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c34c016-0f66-57ab-a126-a8c57998a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470663} {:answer/id #uuid "96c9432e-66dd-5158-98e2-d5639f7d641f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/te