answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3034ba1-2c82-5776-b118-ddbefff303ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-103320" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $L?$\n- **I.** $L∨(¬M∧L)$\n- **II.** $(L∧¬M)∨L$\n- **III.** $(¬M∧L)∨L$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nL∨(L∧¬M)≡L.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $L.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L∨(¬M∧L) & ≡L∨(L∧¬M) \\\\  & ≡L.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $L.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(L∧¬M)∨L & ≡L∨(L∧¬M) \\\\  & ≡L.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $L.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬M∧L)∨L & ≡L∨(¬M∧L) \\\\  & ≡L∨(L∧¬M) \\\\  & ≡L.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07b63c0c-daaa-5f5b-acb3-58d6f36ee869" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Jump Discontinuity on a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73637a49-f6dd-5c31-aec8-f85c2edfe5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470691} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ec72c8-08c3-5a30-8f52-c859ff601865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73637a49-f6dd-5c31-aec8-f85c2edfe5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470691} :answer-field/id #uuid "9760f1fd-b7e1-55fe-8bcd-87df4bfef74d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9917051-93c4-5cda-9370-faa622cfb841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470693} {:answer/id #uuid "e7edb0b5-73cf-5080-9cd1-2d45d6aa0baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7edb0b5-73cf-5080-9cd1-2d45d6aa0baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470694} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b72cb6-3510-5f4a-96d2-f2dc9b753f4d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2474b03-95cc-5d74-bca1-d6adbcc50d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470695} {:answer/id #uuid "f44405da-04b6-51fd-89f4-73e192adf13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2474b03-95cc-5d74-bca1-d6adbcc50d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470695} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0a72084-fa75-53b1-aaf7-92bed01b2f72" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "957e916a-1a46-5f09-b0b4-71f6f746df0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-104666" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca165438c64994306acd6031d5f8e5a0e6d4d0d11a5f6fea8097b19f5105438c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=3$\n- It has a jump discontinuity at $x=3$\n- It is continuous at $x=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(3)=-1$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)=-1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x)=3.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=3$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, II is true, and I and III are false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e476a7e6-9fe8-5985-ab3d-474e04a7980c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470829} {:answer/id #uuid "7af1392e-9bfd-5650-b6c7-cc5983449290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e476a7e6-9fe8-5985-ab3d-474e04a7980c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470829} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa6ab55-2c08-50d9-8d9e-4dda3b96a9e4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fbbc87e-3691-52f5-8ce4-c5cbaad6b748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470831} {:answer/id #uuid "7e31bb92-ac20-5fe1-8af7-bc33a8b119a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e31bb92-ac20-5fe1-8af7-bc33a8b119a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470832} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e97e70a-fdb0-5789-bc5d-9049a1c4f9c7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a2cecd-883c-5851-be4b-db3c4e83d69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470833} {:answer/id #uuid "2b94ed74-766b-54f1-92b2-f5c251317f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16a2cecd-883c-5851-be4b-db3c4e83d69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470833} :answer-field/id #uuid "97b3b63f-64f6-53e3-a996-0684f567a58b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c082af6c-4b35-55f0-b925-7876243430ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-105443" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }3x+y<8,\\,0<x<3\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }0\\le x<6,\\,2<y\\le 4\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<6\\}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3f425a-0a1f-515b-8c03-990715e116f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470835} {:answer/id #uuid "46c61006-9d69-5224-84b5-adb4594d575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c61006-9d69-5224-84b5-adb4594d575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470836} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24fe181-c890-5457-b487-5bd9845a29a6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "455ea2d6-36ea-506e-8abc-4fb2725d1508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470837} {:answer/id #uuid "b1bbc0e3-f77f-5075-b7c1-c24869a40657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "455ea2d6-36ea-506e-8abc-4fb2725d1508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470837} :answer-field/id #uuid "523aebc4-d33b-5507-8bcd-9a008fe77b20" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a53fe6cb-2b4e-5db2-a7b8-cf233dd5a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470839} {:answer/id #uuid "0c743f3a-ed2f-55ac-b5d2-1af41de6baef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a53fe6cb-2b4e-5db2-a7b8-cf233dd5a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470839} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ebafac-d103-5f82-9a2a-34326808b7f4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f4b0cdf-9fe1-57d6-a009-4edf0331d401" :question/math-academy-id "q-105444" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,6\\le x<9,\\,0<y<2}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<3}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(6,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(8,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is also *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee869f7-f725-5bde-a20f-d84176a57341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470847} {:answer/id #uuid "1d73b7d4-fe5d-5d31-9705-14e5c7ac2ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d73b7d4-fe5d-5d31-9705-14e5c7ac2ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470848} :answer-field/id #uuid "8443cc6b-4590-53c1-ba28-2262ff94d030" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283e20ae-0701-5835-9917-a74613735477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470849} {:answer/id #uuid "5d48533d-df16-55a3-bd09-809c8c4e5b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283e20ae-0701-5835-9917-a74613735477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470849} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b626c8a-c307-5508-bb16-8c0338464c78" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09b2211-9c73-5892-89f2-b1430f6074f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470851} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb04f59-6b8b-5f39-bd06-0bc33298c2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d09b2211-9c73-5892-89f2-b1430f6074f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470851} :answer-field/id #uuid "89f298f8-84db-55c2-ac60-1d92591515e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4da29991-8f92-54a5-9016-f20e2647e29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106802" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** you need an umbrella, **then** the sky is not clear.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If the sky is clear, then you do not need an umbrella.\n- **II.** If you do not need an umbrella, then the sky is clear.\n- **III.** If the sky is not clear, then you need an umbrella.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "490995ed-ac99-5768-ad40-5b0e11f10a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471033} {:answer/id #uuid "484cb763-07fa-5ad2-a411-8df07f51dab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490995ed-ac99-5768-ad40-5b0e11f10a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471033} :answer-field/id #uuid "42e6465e-3deb-5f06-abdf-59086e80b9f5" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e74dd853-f834-5489-9ab6-2207e01c886a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471035} {:answer/id #uuid "41a85770-ab01-5832-833b-ff27a5be8436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41a85770-ab01-5832-833b-ff27a5be8436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471036} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b48cb6c-8acd-5de5-896e-2355e9e0e35d" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2269aad-57fb-5cbb-ab49-87e39a9ac7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471037} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f0420b-4735-51ba-ba16-ed5ea138cc6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0f0420b-4735-51ba-ba16-ed5ea138cc6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471038} :answer-field/id #uuid "1807e1b7-7969-53ae-b85d-f2a54b4c14bf" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90365b47-9514-5b9b-bb0b-216780f54607" :question/math-academy-id "q-135487" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0 & 0.5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are nonnegative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.1+0.9=1 \\\\ 0.2+0.8=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are non-negative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0 & 0.5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.5\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.5+0+0.5=1 \\\\ 0+1+0=1 \\\\ 0.5+0+0.5=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$V$ and $W$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16604ddb-69ca-5ace-9dbf-0383a82ea98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471113} {:answer/id #uuid "ed093c42-08ca-5342-9c3d-5d707ac0618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16604ddb-69ca-5ace-9dbf-0383a82ea98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471113} :answer-field/id #uuid "271f6907-9f07-58b0-b69e-9138291c3f29" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be1298c-3ffd-5e63-bdaf-4b61ccf3b37b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471115} {:answer/id #uuid "257b2998-d432-57cf-9773-e11354e3ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "257b2998-d432-57cf-9773-e11354e3ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471116} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c83fa2d-fc72-5a50-960b-e7f3fe4261ae" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472063} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae39a58d-0d80-5e95-a397-418e9ba63826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471117} {:answer/id #uuid "974db8f3-030a-560c-ab7c-a6b736fbe846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974db8f3-030a-560c-ab7c-a6b736fbe846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b5293d9-c7c0-526b-9f08-83692bebc37d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28c149d9-63e5-5d01-abf9-5e8569624b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161639" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,0<y<x}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7519ae6-6283-5e9b-a86d-15f672cad5d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471119} {:answer/id #uuid "18729287-882a-5576-aa4a-14fe49a63438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18729287-882a-5576-aa4a-14fe49a63438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471120} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c5d9db-d0d7-59d7-a450-9db137467fd8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "734986cb-f797-5efd-8757-8769d869f4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471121} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7892cb-fc1c-5d4d-b659-5a1cd819479f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7892cb-fc1c-5d4d-b659-5a1cd819479f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471122} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c231af6-4c3a-595b-b7f7-a6f8e18ec0c9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff0b204-8f86-56a6-929a-934210b283ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471123} {:answer/id #uuid "5a900764-35ba-5f4f-b5a5-cd518fee058c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ff0b204-8f86-56a6-929a-934210b283ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471123} :answer-field/id #uuid "a90ac0c3-b368-5769-b866-780b1af534a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be4d8952-950b-5fb0-a574-0337f64e1d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-161648" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }0<x<3,\\,0<y<6-2x}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }1<x<4,\\,x<y<{x}^{2}}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le {y}^{2}\\le 5}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f311c265-2bb0-5ad1-815d-44417f1e31a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471125} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffdf529-09c7-5cab-a876-7f9b20669834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ffdf529-09c7-5cab-a876-7f9b20669834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471126} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b400c0-9b95-56f2-8848-67709fb87921" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95b0b167-a547-50ff-8123-620fe621a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471127} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c742b0-471f-59d1-924e-69676e078128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95b0b167-a547-50ff-8123-620fe621a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471127} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3cb4bf-3026-5dbf-bb69-ac0bfdbd1d57" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0799b728-a09d-5e7c-a241-f50801a2ea50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471129} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c5826-4aff-5dff-9a12-8d4de0ce361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c5826-4aff-5dff-9a12-8d4de0ce361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471130} :answer-field/id #uuid "26da464c-3c67-5b3b-808a-3b3403f4ed69" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e963f0b-a2c7-5ae0-844a-f3e405d79aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161649" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\ge {y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$\n\nII. $A⊂\\text{int}A$\n\nIII. $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/649c33f1738a35f3d298038bd2cf05d3b435424a4efbbb1e6143cf0d56b2bfd6.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A⊈\\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-\\text{int}A=∂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f435800-2b81-5947-90ad-4a74eb1dee76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471173} {:answer/id #uuid "6727caa3-b8d4-5efd-ad79-327dfcf9a99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f435800-2b81-5947-90ad-4a74eb1dee76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471173} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8a97d97-a433-557a-b652-db4fb249f128" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472092} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da3dfff1-b7cd-50d8-96d9-be0504b46dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471175} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0fa50e-4733-5f26-87e6-0a746393b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a0fa50e-4733-5f26-87e6-0a746393b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471176} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc0c852-246a-5a48-8f9d-dc39d0951ae6" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0540e3ae-15bc-5c25-96ce-77d4312aef86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471177} {:answer/id #uuid "0474c37a-87c9-5fe3-9dae-73199fcc1276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0474c37a-87c9-5fe3-9dae-73199fcc1276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471178} :answer-field/id #uuid "26bfe548-4be8-50f0-b988-9ed0c686fec9" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66e732f7-06d5-591e-98a5-b6812f6bf5f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-174419" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n- **P.** $P:(-2)\\cdot 3$\n- **Q.** $Q:5>3$\n- **R.** $R:7\\in N$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $5$ is larger than  $3.$\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $7$ is a natural number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d607d8-d309-5ca9-83bc-740b4c36bade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471191} {:answer/id #uuid "325fb8bb-d47f-5880-a8b1-b79555ac108d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "325fb8bb-d47f-5880-a8b1-b79555ac108d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471192} :answer-field/id #uuid "42d12dc6-b94a-52d8-8494-2498d1c73f28" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53559d5d-159d-5fdc-bd9d-4e94bdf5ac8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471193} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e30a64-f23f-5094-890c-8e7f4d8a8222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53559d5d-159d-5fdc-bd9d-4e94bdf5ac8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471193} :answer-field/id #uuid "b856be72-7e15-5ad6-945e-6975defb3028" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b52a727-ad5e-5373-9c5a-a0274dde1602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471195} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8607f7-f14a-5008-becc-2bb0c03d4f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc8607f7-f14a-5008-becc-2bb0c03d4f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471196} :answer-field/id #uuid "5def3004-16f9-5b6c-af86-0253fe70b521" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c162f27f-023e-512b-91b9-54632834b487" :question/math-academy-id "q-182238" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n- **I.** $P({R,e})$\n- **II.** $P({x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0})$\n- **III.** $P({(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({R,e})={∅,\\,{R},\\,{e},\\,{R,e}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set II is infinite since the underlying set ${x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0}$  is infinite.\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z}={-1,1},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z})=P({-1,1})={∅,\\,{-1},\\,{1},\\,{-1,1}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aab99129-4a35-5556-a306-b270209eb006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471197} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24b5c-acad-501b-ba57-b7184be25122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24b5c-acad-501b-ba57-b7184be25122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471198} :answer-field/id #uuid "6763cbff-5062-54e7-8246-c7e4594fed34" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef9dd66-3