set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,t,n})={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{t},\\,{n},\\,{Z,t},{Z,n},\\,{t,n},\\,{Z,t,n}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $8.$\n\n- Set II is infinite since the underlying set $Z$ is infinite.\n\n- Set III is infinite since the underlying set ${{2}^{n}∣n\\in Z}$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5c38a40-b0ad-50a0-b1fd-3ca0ed423d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471221} {:answer/id #uuid "b4471eda-3004-561c-b183-28b096dbfdb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5c38a40-b0ad-50a0-b1fd-3ca0ed423d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471221} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c9fc7-d87b-54a3-a66e-faa888700146" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3ed57af-e278-5ede-a755-783ce9ed8c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471223} {:answer/id #uuid "761ff025-d2e6-53d2-985e-4816ac004c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "761ff025-d2e6-53d2-985e-4816ac004c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471224} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9e2ea8-4854-5a7a-8552-15585b54efc9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4f384a-3166-5f09-b657-4055cb82802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471225} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc1fc9d-3e88-590e-be39-355512cb0a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4f384a-3166-5f09-b657-4055cb82802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471225} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34ffd8a-bcff-52d9-a081-61d20b6aec70" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d0274f7-9e96-5c91-af2a-50bf61bf0ba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183341" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $8$ is even **then** $4\\in {2,4,8}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If $4\\in {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is even.\n- **II.** If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even.\n- **III.** If $8$ is not even, then $4\\notin {2,4,8}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement III is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bbc9cee-6d9f-53b6-a3f9-35050e0dd0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471383} {:answer/id #uuid "4f002261-81ab-55ff-af9f-9a2b2a621724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f002261-81ab-55ff-af9f-9a2b2a621724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471384} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a28f8d-5383-5eca-ab07-4ecdbad60269" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26c62176-2c72-5180-a83a-f3021cb5c0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471385} {:answer/id #uuid "059fa7d6-c973-5f8c-b14c-0bf94b31437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "059fa7d6-c973-5f8c-b14c-0bf94b31437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471386} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d943dfd-579b-532f-b5c1-a67bf7f7b2f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b0de36-67f4-5fbd-bc5c-7e6fbd2cc1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471387} {:answer/id #uuid "899f8325-7fc0-5e7f-aed3-fc93ba710d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b0de36-67f4-5fbd-bc5c-7e6fbd2cc1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471387} :answer-field/id #uuid "f68de2b5-cce3-546e-85e3-13db4ede6900" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec98e74e-e68c-5045-a599-d3ec1260eaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-330299" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n- **I.** ${x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- **II.** $-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- **III.** $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=1\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{{x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2a88b9c-22ee-5b00-af09-d1cdae976ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471389} {:answer/id #uuid "699c223a-b0f1-5ab1-9742-cc8cc24e7610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2a88b9c-22ee-5b00-af09-d1cdae976ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471389} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe7b73e-c8d1-5806-97dd-83443a307c30" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f77fbd2-8e41-54f7-8dab-495bfe9057db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471391} {:answer/id #uuid "b928d8c6-5415-580d-a8fc-bfe309b7a281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f77fbd2-8e41-54f7-8dab-495bfe9057db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471391} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc36a6ef-b56b-5871-97f4-e7173861f357" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5134166f-f275-568c-8bbb-42b5f7da138d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471393} {:answer/id #uuid "37b63443-245b-500c-9c9b-3ed20a0c4b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b63443-245b-500c-9c9b-3ed20a0c4b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471394} :answer-field/id #uuid "07370987-e91d-5a14-9c0b-88a34bdf1ab6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "028e3468-5c29-5e67-a28b-97b2d534ac0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-330306" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n- **I.** ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$\n- **II.** $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$\n- **III.** $-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $-1$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option III is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a9f9cf-06f6-51b8-ba41-a8b6300a5c2b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordinary and Singular Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c540cb1b-69f7-5f99-bad5-ce4fb3967ef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471435} {:answer/id #uuid "53b186d2-81f0-5610-928c-351f854cf04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b186d2-81f0-5610-928c-351f854cf04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471436} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5fd9f56-7c1c-5e45-b553-b8266c8209ea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472223} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8441d8c-043c-5a17-9a39-6a5dea8a1934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471437} {:answer/id #uuid "59044e28-9bad-5f71-afa3-7e02f334e2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59044e28-9bad-5f71-afa3-7e02f334e2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471438} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7bf0c61-d4ff-567d-8e2b-5981962d2d56" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7c0fbf-2b18-5fad-bedf-cab28bfd9c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471439} {:answer/id #uuid "c1eb06ad-9786-5477-89a2-338126df89db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c7c0fbf-2b18-5fad-bedf-cab28bfd9c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471439} :answer-field/id #uuid "94df1425-9126-5127-93c1-dfb7144e6014" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff653b13-8b67-5277-ad4c-9f98277f418a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342282" :question/problem "$$\nx(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+4y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a **singular** point of the differential equation above?\n- **I.** $x=-3$\n- **II.** $x=0$\n- **III.** $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both coefficients $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $x(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+4y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-2}{x(x+3)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{4}{x(x+3)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-2}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{4}{x(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-3,$ since both denominators at $x=-3$ equal zero. So, $x=-3$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=0,$ since both denominators at $x=0$ equal zero. So, $x=0$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5772d6f-b4c4-5b0f-a341-7bcce7c53ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471441} {:answer/id #uuid "72f28384-9464-531f-83ec-b7d7d44da974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5772d6f-b4c4-5b0f-a341-7bcce7c53ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471441} :answer-field/id #uuid "3de9898a-65aa-5f5c-a471-68d4884d2a25" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f34e0f7-5c36-57be-8be0-72cd026a3c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471443} {:answer/id #uuid "545a20a3-dc0a-54e0-a437-92e4bb0d8db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f34e0f7-5c36-57be-8be0-72cd026a3c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471443} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e5ae857-3730-5c76-9614-b81b46af3e2a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "331a7444-e6ed-5b95-9c85-51c56d8adc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471445} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd04662-64d9-59d1-be58-90ecddce155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dd04662-64d9-59d1-be58-90ecddce155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471446} :answer-field/id #uuid "377eb8bf-59f3-5a09-928e-03ed7443b513" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39331851-2b44-5819-96f4-7d54c8cd9bd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342366" :question/problem "$$\n(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$\n- **II.** The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$\n- **III.** The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{x+3}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=-3,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=-3.$ So, statement I is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x+3)P(x)=(x+3)\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\n is *not* analytic about $x=-3$ since its denominator vanishes at $x=-3.$ Therefore, statement II is false.\n\n- Since statement I is false, $x=-3$ is a singular point. Also, since statement II is false, it follows that $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point. Thus, statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5582e4fd-2c1b-5d7e-8c00-e97e06814dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471447} {:answer/id #uuid "a3eb097d-ca23-5819-ac10-dc59c55d7b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3eb097d-ca23-5819-ac10-dc59c55d7b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471448} :answer-field/id #uuid "d03efb8d-a67e-5194-9397-44b10a9fe206" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398cb7dd-8121-5f92-b1f8-3cb5dfa077bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471449} {:answer/id #uuid "835ea12a-0dec-59ad-8c9d-1e2c535804ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "398cb7dd-8121-5f92-b1f8-3cb5dfa077bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471449} :answer-field/id #uuid "671dd875-2b17-5bf5-8cd4-e539f182cfa9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472230} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c761f2b5-ba81-5508-8846-69bc0e2a0948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471451} {:answer/id #uuid "e051646c-5725-58cc-bba2-10290a7faee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c761f2b5-ba81-5508-8846-69bc0e2a0948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471451} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac6ae07c-0a83-5d77-ab7d-cfed78b60de1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "036af2f8-8d3f-5a9f-9714-c21bb558dc15" :question/math-academy-id "q-35538" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=4x-3y-1$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=-1$ gives a line\n- **II.** $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$\n- **III.** $c=2$ gives a parabola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y-1 & =c \\\\ 4x-3y-(c+1) & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{3}x-\\frac{c+1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3},$ which is a line different to the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x-1,$ which is not a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d046747a-b317-586d-8d55-5c90d106b70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471459} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ae2f16-5c4b-5f1c-bc31-c6238c4fb198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d046747a-b317-586d-8d55-5c90d106b70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471459} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01cb9ca-cfef-5a04-b8e8-faaa3c67d474" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8627-87dd-5f0d-836a-c310a9c4ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471461} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf51cce-838b-5461-8589-29027a79ad48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8627-87dd-5f0d-836a-c310a9c4ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471461} :answer-field/id #uuid "9af77a4f-7777-5db4-b47d-afe23125eeb7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aadc0f6-aa90-5bee-94bc-57244da99e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471463} {:answer/id #uuid "46907805-5ba1-518e-903b-c1d4d29ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46907805-5ba1-518e-903b-c1d4d29ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471464} :answer-field/id #uuid "af943ca9-e995-586e-81d8-b5176e4f024d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3aaf864-2fae-5bdc-a851-6e2a3303364c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71398" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=0$ gives a circle\n- **II.** $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n- **III.** $c=2$ gives a parabola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2y & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a circle.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49cf872d-689f-5e2e-9332-695ac6faa1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471483} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b69705-0fc5-56cf-9a35-6c357cb97eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0b69705-0fc5-56cf-9a35-6c357cb97eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471484} :answer-field/id #uuid "68f67652-3fb0-559a-89e4-313feeaf26f0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54aa25bf-5940-59e0-a6aa-ae17ece3e229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471485} {:answer/id #uuid "72bc58dc-bdb3-5d78-b56d-a3ff427f2c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72bc58dc-bdb3-5d78-b56d-a3ff427f2c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471486} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c956b2c-afaf-5232-8dd1-6441df297688" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc3df3f-0a2f-58b6-8cc0-dd5b0c759bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471487} {:answer/id #uuid "694f2513-41e1-5b51-8e18-a72cf04d9069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc3df3f-0a2f-58b6-8cc0-dd5b0c759bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471487} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4377199-a8d0-5db1-a161-0f59b2917c34" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4218ace-9c46-5876-8096-9bc751d57412" :question/math-academy-id "q-71793" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $[-2,2]$\n\nII. $[3,9]$\n\nIII. $[-1,1)\\cup (3,4]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-2,2]$ and $[3,9]$ are closed because:\n\n- The boundary points of $[-2,2]$ are $-2$, and $2.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of $[3,9]$ are $3$, and $9.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not closed because $[-1,1)\\cup (3,4]$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a89a159-240f-5646-9d9d-07e5c88ba649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471489} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1f9b96-8b9d-594b-8ea8-d5a1eaad1bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a89a159-240f-5646-9d9d-07e5c88ba649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471489} :answer-field/id #uuid "0833ee3c-9acf-5297-a02c-1e4717cd5fa6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b98336f7-7572-56ff-ab79-2163035ae7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471491} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4108d2-001c-59cf-a66b-bc536879029e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef4108d2-001c-59cf-a66b-bc536879029e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471492} :answer-field/id #uuid "02bbcb49-82f4-560f-8987-ae979c8010d1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4d8016a-4094-5433-b699-428b874f7c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471493} {:answer/id #uuid "28ae6bd1-0410-5e04-9b95-9fb08176b892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d8016a-4094-5433-b699-428b874f7c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471493} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7a8e272-8e29-5c30-abd0-98186c11ca59" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c4a042d-b417-5a76-bd5b-ca2066d08ead" :question/math-academy-id "q-71795" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n- **I.** $(-3,1)$\n- **II.** $[0,2]\\cup [6,7]$\n- **III.** $(-1,3)\\cup (4,7]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[0,2]\\cup [6,7]$ is closed. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $0,2,6,$ and $7.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(-3,1)$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(-1,3)\\cup (4,7]$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed61332-13c7-5cfe-bd7d-b74b4269a49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471495} {:answer/id #uuid "62d38bc3-1662-5473-abf7-d55153533159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed61332-13c7-5cfe-bd7d-b74b4269a49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471495} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3655b78-dca0-5c5f-a7ea-0a3af751b3aa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4d94e16-9fb4-52f5-9a9b-20b703166ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471497} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc95394-94f6-5088-8810-45fb26d96dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cc95394-94f6-5088-8810-45fb26d96dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471498} :answer-field/id #uuid "96c3ea74-ebd2-5dec-87e2-24f8023a937c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472254} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c876fa-21cc-5454-a21e-c57b437cf7e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471499} {:answer/id #uuid "d9451c20-32c4-5438-8d6e-4fcbccc418b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9451c20-32c4-5438-8d6e-4fcbccc418b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471500} :answer-field/id #uuid "01edc11e-256d-5617-a357-b21be324d896" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9b6f2b8-c18f-5a12-b634-f89ac5f5481f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71796" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n- **I.** $(6,10]$\n- **II.** $[2,5]$\n- **III.** $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[2,5]$ and $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ are closed because:\n\n- The boundary points of $[2,5]$ are $2$ and $5.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ are $0,1,3,$ and $4.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not closed because $(6,10]$ has a boundary point $6$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d0a02e-b9a7-5533-ba1a-2f80acfdd774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471501} {:answer/id #uuid "3634b9a6-d22a-5361-aa5e-75a49f2a1180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d0a02e-b9a7-5533-ba1a-2f80acfdd774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471501} :answer-field/id #uuid "6abbef18-93ea-56dd-b268-7018d23ddfa8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f8f10a7-0a63-5ee4-bf6e-1ee054e2c178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471503} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6d0c4f-4b1a-5d9e-9cdc-49d1f07cf01e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f8f10a7-0a63-5ee4-bf6e-1ee054e2c178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471503} :answer-field/id #uuid "f04b2162-9644-5318-a58f-b073768907c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da2799fe-1894-5db5-bc3f-8d59a60ca339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471505} {:answer/id #uuid "97dfe6de-be4b-5960-b11e-8aa543d47602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97dfe6de-be4b-5960-b11e-8aa543d47602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471506} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6f3acd4-15de-55a8-9779-2caa89a1cd1c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0cdf362-49b4-5e81-91f4-944c2a137d99" :question/math-academy-id "q-71801" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(-2,1]\\cup [3,9)$\n\nII. $[4,6)\\cup (9,11)$\n\nIII. $(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$ is open. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $-1$, $4$, $6$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(-2,1]\\cup [3,9)$ has four boundary points $-2$, $1$, $3$, and $9$, and the points $1$ and $3$ lie in the set.\n\n- $[4,6)\\cup (9,11)$ has four boundary points $4$, $6$, $9$, and $11$, and the point $4$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e815afe7-e4a5-5591-9f0e-2bf26f3075b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471669} {:answer/id #uuid "d75542aa-7263-5d8d-b51a-d9df54c992a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e815afe7-e4a5-5591-9f0e-2bf26f3075b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471669} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7dcfed-0835-5f2a-a484-e51cc3784d92" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19efdde4-e8a8-57ef-b8cd-2e6daeb6231a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471671} {:answer/id #uuid "541c39ec-dfcb-5f4e-b641-2498e75c6b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "541c39ec-dfcb-5f4e-b641-2498e75c6b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471672} :answer-field/id #uuid "dadb9685-5531-5d90-9da3-34529ac942d4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5f9bcaf-a69c-5760-9bb5-b9f9e9c51c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471673} {:answer/id #uuid "faf64540-f9e0-59af-8fe6-792306c1dc9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faf64540-f9e0-59af-8fe6-792306c1dc9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471674} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e6f530-6801-54f7-b77e-828d18b79824" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1b738de-914d-5dd9-b0ba-d383cdcec6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-81718" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $Q?$\n- **I.** $¬R∧(Q∧¬R)$\n- **II.** $Q∧(¬R∨Q)$\n- **III.** $(¬R∨Q)∧Q$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nQ∧(Q∨¬R)≡Q.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $Q.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $Q.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q∧(¬R∨Q) & ≡Q∧(Q∨¬R) \\\\  & ≡Q.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $Q.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬R∨Q)∧Q & ≡Q∧(Q∨¬R) \\\\  & ≡Q.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157275 :knowledge-point/id #