:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471686} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe09b33-73e1-5d48-a50b-f6511ccdf629" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c524db33-b009-501a-aa7b-2de183456b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81722" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $M?$\n- **I.** $M∨(N∨M)$\n- **II.** $(M∧N)∨M$\n- **III.** $M∨(N∧M)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nM∨(M∧N)≡M.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $M.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(M∧N)∨M & ≡M∨(M∧N) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M∨(N∧M) & ≡M∨(M∧N) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a995511-c3ab-56a2-a302-1bedfa2904eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471747} {:answer/id #uuid "6107507d-d229-5b6d-bb78-6dd1692778b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6107507d-d229-5b6d-bb78-6dd1692778b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471748} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd7e4d8b-e538-50ff-8391-7016b9eb8aa4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a56ffb3-32e1-5ba6-b9d2-390da306e6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471749} {:answer/id #uuid "daaaceb5-1235-586b-9abe-50131f6df41e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a56ffb3-32e1-5ba6-b9d2-390da306e6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471749} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b29eaa7-fd58-579d-814b-190372ed2a71" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbda4a9-a5b8-5487-bcc5-bf76150369a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471751} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc52945-efa3-5eae-946e-3e2073cc7990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dbda4a9-a5b8-5487-bcc5-bf76150369a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471751} :answer-field/id #uuid "462f3da3-0d78-500c-8d71-92f10c5cbc0a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b3cb87d-282a-5d16-9402-d3db5936c8ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-82660" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** I am not sleeping, **then** I am awake.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If I am not awake, then I am sleeping.\n- **II.** If I am sleeping, then I am not awake.\n- **III.** If I am awake, then I am not sleeping.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
